Subject: vmm hold the host's Vulkan driver loaded while the renderer lives
Why: AC-T7.4.1: the render server serves each Venus context as a thread of the GPU VM process, and each context opens the host's Vulkan loader and makes an instance of it, closing both as it goes; nothing held the host's driver between contexts, so the loader loaded it anew for every context, and NVIDIA's libnvidia-tls (DF_STATIC_TLS) took static TLS on each load, which glibc never gives back. Reproduced on 00aad (RTX 5060 Ti, 620.70.06, VM 2 vCPU/1024 MiB): the guest Program's 19th run in one VM failed at vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices with VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED, 3 of 3 VMs and ROOT's census, and the host loader said 'libnvidia-tls.so.620.70.06: cannot allocate memory in static TLS block', 'Failed to detect any valid GPUs'. host_visible's instance is now kept as the renderer's HeldDriver and dropped after it. Test a_contexts_instance_loads_no_static_tls_driver_anew_while_the_renderer_holds_it: red on the original (libGLX_nvidia, libnvidia-glcore, libnvidia-tls loaded anew), green with the hold.

